the missing number?\n\n{{field-1}}\n$%$ of $2=6$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the given problem as the following product:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%\\times 2=6\n$$\n\nUsing the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%=6÷2=\\frac{6}{2}\n$$\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{2}=\\frac{6\\times 50}{2\\times 50}=\\frac{300}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{300}{100}=300\\,%\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455489 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147574 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e81c1d02-c62a-59e9-9c15-66ec632802da" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Percentage Given Two Numbers Using Simplification"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c00539cb-4e19-5ee7-9dce-b65ad4e45642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c00539cb-4e19-5ee7-9dce-b65ad4e45642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455232} :answer-field/id #uuid "173b46a0-52f2-51a5-9db7-2ae7f3e86440" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bbef286c-e7f0-513c-aea2-c85d78514b95" :question/math-academy-id "q-185152" :question/problem "What is the missing number?\n\n$28\\,\\times $\n{{field-1}}\n$%=7$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the given problem as the following product:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%\\times 28=7\n$$\n\nUsing the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%=7÷28=\\frac{7}{28}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{28}=\\frac{7÷7}{28÷7}=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1\\times 25}{4\\times 25}=\\frac{25}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{25}{100}=25\\,%\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455475 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147573 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2cfba3f-e03a-5cf2-8f7d-9b5576c8eb91" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Percentage Given Two Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "250b7190-cdbb-5d32-b51b-b93844676a68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454960} {:answer/id #uuid "4960e0dc-4a2a-5127-9a54-50c9b5898315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455027} {:answer/id #uuid "7112fd4e-0fe7-50b8-acd2-d1dd64c5c185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455114} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ade847-5a50-56c1-b95c-3754185f0121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455248} {:answer/id #uuid "d58400ea-a4d2-5e83-9e0b-4702151398e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8ade847-5a50-56c1-b95c-3754185f0121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455248} :answer-field/id #uuid "f074260e-1161-5ec2-9b60-862ec3681ab9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "87a9ebe9-f422-5f29-8cbc-96b3a193eef9" :question/math-academy-id "q-60920" :question/problem "What is the missing number?\n\n$\\,$ $\\boxed{}\\,%$ of $5=3$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the given problem as the following product:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%\\times 5=3\n$$\n\nUsing the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%=3÷5=\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{3\\times 20}{5\\times 20}=\\frac{60}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{60}{100}=60%\n$$"}]}
